<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lincolnshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lincolnshire is a large county in the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humber">Humber</a> estuary to the Wash. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> it was part of the territory of the Corieltauvi, and its northern part later formed the Anglian kingdom of Lindsey before falling under Mercia and then Danish settlement. It is mostly low-lying farmland, with the Wolds and the Fens, and its county town is Lincoln.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lincolnshire.jpg" alt="Lincolnshire" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tilman2007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1388680_Cathedral_Church_of_St_Mary,_West_Front_Lincoln_20240519_0252.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
